  "requestTimestamp": "2026-07-19T06:04:41.651Z",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nAn individual with ₱250,000 gross compensation income in 2024 is not required to file an income tax return.\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThis is based on Section 51-A of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), which states that individuals receiving purely compensation income from only one employer, where the income tax has been correctly withheld, are not required to file an annual income tax return.\n\n### Interpretation\nSection 51-A of the NIRC allows for substituted filing of income tax returns for employees whose income tax has been withheld correctly by their employer. Since the gross compensation income of ₱250,000 falls within the threshold where no tax is due (0% tax rate), and assuming the employer has withheld the correct amount, the individual is exempt from filing.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor practical purposes, this means that if the individual’s only source of income is from a single employer and the employer has complied with withholding tax requirements, the individual can rely on the employer's withholding certificate as sufficient documentation for tax purposes, thus simplifying their tax obligations for the year.",
